title: Home_Intro
---
Osaka, July. Even the cicadas sound tired of the heat.
For a week now, you've woken at exactly three in the morning.
And every time, there's snow outside the window. Deep, silent snow, in the middle of summer.
The glass is cold enough to sting. Your breath fogs in your own room.
By morning it's gone. The street is hot and loud again, and nobody else saw a thing.
Tonight, when it comes back, you're going out there.
===
title: Night_First
---
Three in the morning. This time, you open the door.
The cold goes straight through your pyjamas.
The street is buried. Not a sound, not even wind.
Past the snow, the road runs on further than you can see.
===
title: Home_GearHint
---
You wake with your fingers still aching from the cold.
Pyjamas won't get you far out there. Somewhere in this city, someone must still sell a winter coat in July.
===
title: Ending
---
You sink into the armchair. The heat soaks into your hands, your face, your bones.
Through the melting frost, the street is still white.
Someone is standing out there in the snow, under the dead streetlight, facing the window.
They lift a hand, slowly, as if they've been waiting for you.
<<if met("flag:aoi_knows")>>
Aoi's grandmother said the ones who see the snow always come back. Mostly.
<<endif>>
<<if met("flag:kenta_confided")>>
You'll tell Kenta everything, like you promised. Maybe then he'll call his brother.
<<endif>>
Your eyes close before you can wave back.
<<end_game "You wake to cicadas. It's summer again.">>
===
